{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"JLSEC-2026-1079","published":"2026-07-30T16:02:27.435Z","modified":"2026-07-30T18:35:45.222122685Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-62343","EUVD-2026-50572","GHSA-f5m7-cqgw-8hm7"],"summary":"ImageMagick: Heap Buffer Over-Write in morphology operation when an invalid kernel is provided","details":"ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. In versions prior to 6.9.13-51 and 7.0.1-0 and above prior to 7.1.2-26, an invalid kernel can cause a heap buffer over-write when performing a morphology operation with a user supplied kernel. This issue has been fixed in versions 6.9.13-51 and 7.1.2-26.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/ImageMagick_jll?uuid=c73af94c-d91f-53ed-93a7-00f77d67a9d7"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.1.2028+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1079.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-f5m7-cqgw-8hm7"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-f5m7-cqgw-8hm7"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/dlemstra/Magick.NET/releases/tag/14.15.0"}],"database_specific":{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","sources":[{"database_specific":{"status":"Received"},"html_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-62343","id":"CVE-2026-62343","imported":"2026-07-30T14:09:43.475Z","modified":"2026-07-30T00:16:24.200Z","published":"2026-07-30T00:16:24.200Z","url":"https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0?cveId=CVE-2026-62343"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-f5m7-cqgw-8hm7","id":"GHSA-f5m7-cqgw-8hm7","imported":"2026-07-30T14:10:40.062Z","modified":"2026-07-24T16:19:54Z","published":"2026-07-24T16:19:53Z","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-f5m7-cqgw-8hm7"},{"html_url":"https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/E